---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_268",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 268,
  "text": "[[1041.4]] <b>222₃.  Demonstratio reperta DEMONSTRATIO REPERTA\n[[1041.6]] <b>Demonstratio pure Analytica</b>\n [[1041.7]] <b>Quod in multiplicatione ─ in ─ faciat +</b> </p>\n<p> [[1041.8]] Sit quantitas <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> multiplicanda in aliam <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i> ajo multiplicationem fieri hoc modo:\n [[1041.9]] ^&.bb <Leibniz special character><tab/>+ <i>x^#'2</i> <tab/>─ <i>b</i><tab/><i>x</i>^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/><i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i>\n [[1041.10]] <tab/><i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i>\n [[1041.11]] <tab/>^#6+─ <i>cx</i> + <i>bc</i>^#6-\n [[1041.12]] <tab/>+ <i>x^#'2</i> <tab/>─ <i>bx</i> NB.\n [[1041.13]] Manifesta autem est pars multiplicationis <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>cx</i>, quaeritur solum an admitti possit\n[[1041.14]] ─ <i>b</i> in ─ <i>c</i> dare + <i>bc</i>. Quod sic ostendo: </p>\n<p> [[1041.15]] Primum ponatur <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>, ergo etiam erit <i>x</i> + <i>c</i> aequ. <i>b</i> + <i>c</i>. Ergo <i>x^#'2</i> + <i>xc</i> aequ.\n[[1041.16]] <i>bx</i> + <i>cx</i> multiplicatis scilicet omnibus per <i>x</i>. Et pro <i>xc</i> ponendo <i>bc</i> (quia <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>), fiet\n[[1041.17]] <i>x^#'2</i> + <i>bc</i> aequ. <i>bx</i> + <i>cx</i> sive fiet: </p>\n<p> [[1041.18]] <i>x^#'2</i> <tab/>─ <i>bx</i> + <i>bc aequ. 0</i>.\n [[1041.19]] <tab/>─ <i>cx</i> </p>\n<p> [[1042.1]] Jam si multiplicetur x - b per x - c, prodibit <Fn>^&.bb <Leibniz special character><tab/>+<i>x^#'2</i> <tab/>─<tab/> <i>bx</i> <tab/>─ <i>b</i>^&.b</i> <Leibniz special character> <tab/>+<i>x</i> <tab/>─ <i>b</i> <tab/>+<i>x</i> <tab/>─ <i>c</i> <tab/>^#6+─ <i>cx</i> <tab/>+<greek>U</greek>^#6- <tab/>+<i>x^#'2</i> <tab/>─ <i>bx</i></Fn>\n [[1042.2]] <i>x^#'2</i> <tab/>─ <i>bx</i> + <greek>U</greek> <i>aequ. 0</i>.\n [[1042.3]] <tab/>─ <i>cx</i> </p>\n<p> [[1042.4]] Nam si id quod <i>nihilo</i> aequale est (hoc loco <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i>) multiplices per quidvis productum\n[[1042.5]] etiam <i>nihilo</i> aequale erit. Hinc conferendo has duas aequationes invicem necessario fit\n[[1042.6]] <i>bc</i> aequ. <greek>U</greek>, adeoque ─ <i>b</i> in ─ <i>c</i> dedit <greek>U</greek> seu + <i>bc</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1042.7]] Quod autem processit posito <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>, procedet etiam in alia multiplicatione\n[[1042.8]] quacunque, ut facile patet, nam sit <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> multiplicanda per <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i>. Utique poterimus facere\n[[1042.9]] <i>d</i> aequ. <i>e</i> + <i>x</i> (quia <i>d</i> est major quam <i>x</i>, adeoque et major quam <i>b</i>, posito <i>x</i> aequ. <i>b</i>) et fiet:\n[[1042.10]] <i>e</i> + <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> multiplicanda per <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i>, et necessario fiet productum\n[[1042.11]] <i>ex</i> ─ <i>ec</i> + <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> + <i>bc</i>. Fit enim utique <i>ex</i> ─ <i>ec</i> + <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> · <greek>U</greek>. Quod tantundem\n[[1042.12]] esse debet quod <i>ex</i> ─ <i>ec</i> (quia <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> aequ. <i>0</i>, ergo <i>e</i> + <i>x</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i> idem quod <i>e</i> in <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i>).\n[[1042.13]] Ergo <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> + <greek>U</greek> aequ. <i>0</i>, ergo ut supra <greek>U</greek> aequ. + <i>bc</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1042.14]] Jam ostendemus idem fieri debuisse etsi <i>d</i> fuisset retenta nec per <i>x</i> explicata quia\n[[1042.15]] peracta per <i>d</i> multiplicatione utique postea explicare licet <i>d</i> per <i>e</i> + <i>x</i>. Nimirum ­ostendimus\n[[1042.16]] <i>ex</i> ─ <i>ec</i> + <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> + <i>bc</i> esse aequ. <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i>. Jam <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in <i>x</i> aequ.\n[[1042.17]] <i>ex</i> + <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> (ob valorem ipsius <i>d</i>) et <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in - <i>c</i> aequ. ─ <i>dc</i> · <greek>U</greek>, id est (quia <i>d</i> aequ. <i>e</i> + <i>x</i>)\n[[1042.18]] <i>d</i> ─ <i>b</i> in ─ <i>c</i> aequ. ─ <i>ec</i> ─ <i>xc</i> · <greek>U</greek>. Ergo summa collecta <i>ex</i> + <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>ec</i> ─ <i>xc</i> · <greek>U</greek> aequale\n[[1042.19]] superiori <i>ex</i> ─ <i>ec</i> + <i>x^#'2</i> ─ <i>bx</i> ─ <i>cx</i> + <i>bc</i>. Ergo ablatis utriaque iisdem fiet <greek>U</greek> aequ. + <i>bc</i>. </p>\n<p> [[1042.20]] Breviorem hanc demonstrationem reddidissem si vacasset. Facile etiam patet idem\n[[1042.21]] fore et si adhibuissemus non <i>x</i> ─ <i>c</i> sed aliam quamvis ut <i>f</i> ─ <i>c</i>. </p>\n",
  "number": "222₃.",
  "title": "Demonstratio reperta",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:222₃. Demonstratio reperta DEMONSTRATIO REPERTA Demonstratio pure Analytica Quod in multiplicatione ─ in ─ faciat + Sit quantitas x ─ b multiplicanda in aliam x ─ c ajo multiplicationem fieri hoc modo: ^&.bb + x^#'2 ─ bx^&.b x ─ b x ─ c ^#6+─ cx + bc^#6- + x^#'2 ─ bx NB. Manifesta autem est pars mul...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>